{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And He said, For I will be with you</b>, <b>and you shall come to Pharaoh</b>, <b>and you shall bring out the children of Israel</b>, <b>and behold, I have given you a sign that I have sent you</b>. The sense of <b>that you shall bring them out</b> is that they shall serve Me on this mountain, on which I showed you this great vision. Thus Scripture says: \"who brought you out of the land of Egypt to be to you for an Elohim\" (Leviticus 22:33). And likewise Moses said to Pharaoh: \"a journey of three days we shall go in the wilderness and sacrifice to YHWH our Elohim\" (below 5:3 [5:23]), for this is the distance between ancient Egypt and Mount Sinai — only that Israel, when they went out, did not take the road through the land of the Philistines, and furthermore because they stayed in one place many days, as I shall explain. And this is what Scripture says: \"and he built an altar beneath the mountain, and they brought up burnt offerings and sacrificed peace offerings\" (below 24:4 [24:5]). Then a covenant was made with Israel that they should be to HaShem for a people, and He would be to them for an Elohim."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The two parenthetical verse citations marked למטה (below) appear with chapter-verse numbers that are off by one from the Hebrew verse division; Ibn Ezra cites by the Hebrew verse count, here normalized to standard chapter:verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:20.402885827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}